## Driver Structure

### Layer 1: Pure Virtual Interface

**Location**: `include/alpacacore/<device>_driver.h`

This already exists! You don't need to modify it. Example:

```cpp
// include/alpacacore/camera_driver.h
class CameraDriver : public AlpacaDriver {
public:
    virtual ~CameraDriver() = default;
    virtual void start_exposure(double duration, bool light) = 0;
    virtual ImageArray get_image_array() const = 0;
    // ... more methods
};
```

### Layer 2: SDK Wrapper

**Location**: `include/alpacacore/vendor/<vendor>/<vendor>_sdk_wrapper.h`

Create a clean C++ interface that wraps the messy SDK:

```cpp
// include/alpacacore/vendor/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.h
#pragma once

#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <memory>

namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo {

// Clean types - no SDK types exposed
struct ZWOCameraInfo {
    int camera_id;
    std::string name;
    int max_width;
    int max_height;
    bool is_color;
};

class ZWOSDKWrapper {
public:
    static ZWOSDKWrapper& instance();
    
    // Clean API - hides SDK complexity
    std::vector<ZWOCameraInfo> enumerate_cameras();
    bool open_camera(int camera_id);
    void close_camera();
    bool start_exposure(int camera_id, double duration_seconds, bool light);
    bool is_exposure_ready(int camera_id);
    std::vector<uint8_t> get_image_data(int camera_id, int& width, int& height);
    
private:
    // SDK-specific implementation details hidden
    class Impl;
    std::unique_ptr<Impl> pimpl_;
};

} // namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo
```

**Implementation**: `src/vendors/<vendor>/<vendor>_sdk_wrapper.cpp`

```cpp
// src/vendors/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.cpp
#include <alpacacore/vendor/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.h>
#include <ASICamera2.h>  // Only place SDK header is included!

namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo {

class ZWOSDKWrapper::Impl {
    // SDK-specific implementation
};

ZWOSDKWrapper& ZWOSDKWrapper::instance() {
    static ZWOSDKWrapper wrapper;
    return wrapper;
}

// Implement methods using SDK...
std::vector<ZWOCameraInfo> ZWOSDKWrapper::enumerate_cameras() {
    // Use ASICamera2 SDK here
}

} // namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo
```

### Layer 3: Driver Implementation

**Location**: `src/vendors/<vendor>/<vendor>_<device>_driver.cpp`

Implement the pure virtual interface using the wrapper:

```cpp
// src/vendors/zwo/zwo_camera_driver.cpp
#include <alpacacore/camera_driver.h>
#include <alpacacore/vendor/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.h>
#include <alpacacore/util/error_handling.h>
#include <alpacacore/util/logging.h>

namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo {

class ZWOCameraDriver : public CameraDriver {
public:
    ZWOCameraDriver(int camera_id, int device_number);
    ~ZWOCameraDriver() override;
    
    // Implement CameraDriver interface
    void start_exposure(double duration, bool light) override {
        auto& sdk = ZWOSDKWrapper::instance();
        if (!sdk.start_exposure(camera_id_, duration, light)) {
            throw AlpacaException("Failed to start exposure");
        }
    }
    
    ImageArray get_image_array() const override {
        auto& sdk = ZWOSDKWrapper::instance();
        int width, height;
        auto data = sdk.get_image_data(camera_id_, width, height);
        
        ImageArray img;
        img.data = std::move(data);
        img.width = width;
        img.height = height;
        img.rank = 2; // Monochrome
        return img;
    }
    
    // Implement all other CameraDriver methods...
    
private:
    int camera_id_;
    // ... other state
};

} // namespace alpacacore::vendor::zwo
```

