## Step-by-Step Driver Implementation

### Step 1: Create Wrapper Header

```bash
# Create wrapper header
mkdir -p include/alpacacore/vendor/zwo
touch include/alpacacore/vendor/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.h
```

Write the wrapper interface (see Layer 2 example above).

### Step 2: Implement Wrapper

```bash
# Create wrapper implementation
touch src/vendors/zwo/zwo_sdk_wrapper.cpp
```

Implement using PIMPL pattern to hide SDK details.

### Step 3: Implement Driver

```bash
# Create driver implementation
touch src/vendors/zwo/zwo_camera_driver.cpp
```

Implement all pure virtual methods from `CameraDriver`.

### Step 4: Create Factory Function

```cpp
// In zwo_camera_driver.cpp or separate header
std::unique_ptr<CameraDriver> create_zwo_camera(int device_number, int camera_id) {
    return std::make_unique<ZWOCameraDriver>(camera_id, device_number);
}
```

### Step 5: Configure CMake

See [CMake Configuration](#cmake-configuration) section below.

